        role: "Veterinarian",
        exam: [.direct("Please tell the jury about your job.", "\"I'm a veterinarian. I treat small animals and perform necropsies when an animal dies suddenly or unexpectedly.\""), .direct("What happened to the four cats?", "\"They were brought in within a few hours of each other, vomiting and shaking. Three died at my clinic and one died on the way.\""), .direct("What did the necropsy show?", "\"Antifreeze poisoning. The kidneys showed the classic crystals and damage. It's a cruel way for an animal to die.\""), .direct("What did you find in the cats' stomachs?", "\"Fish, which tested positive for ethylene glycol. Someone had mixed it into the fish.\""), .direct("Where was the fish found?", "\"Deputies found tainted fish in {D}'s trash can and in a plastic bag near the fence.\""), .direct("What did {DL} say about the cats?", "\"That the cats had been in {D.his} yard and bothered {D.him}. {D.He} said {D.he} had complained to {V}.\""), .cross("Could anyone have left the fish near the fence?", "\"Yes. The fence was open, and the fish could have been left by anyone.\""), .cross("Was {DL}'s trash open?", "\"The deputies told me the lid was off. I wasn't there.\""), .cross("Did you test the fish in the trash?", "\"Yes. It had the same chemical, but I can't say who put it there.\""), .cross("Did any witness see {DL} leave fish?", "\"Not that I know of.\""), .cross("Did {DL} express regret after the cats died?", "\"Yes. {D.He} said {D.he} was sorry for the loss.\"")],
        theory: ("{D}, a neighbor who had complained about the cats, poisoned four of them with antifreeze left in fish.", "A stranger left the tainted fish near the open fence, and {DL} never touched the cats."),
