        openings: ("Four cats owned by {V} died after eating fish tainted with antifreeze near a fence. A necropsy confirmed the poison, tainted fish was found in {D}'s trash, and {DL} came through this court in {PRIORDATE} in the case known as {PRIOR}.", "{DL} says {D.he} complained about the cats but never poisoned them. The defense will show that {D.his} trash was open to anyone, and that a stranger could have left the fish near the fence."),
        closings: ("Four cats died of antifreeze poisoning, and tainted fish was in {D}'s trash. {D} had complained about the cats. Back in {PRIORDATE}, {DL} was a defendant in this court for {PRIOR}.", "{D} complained, but never poisoned anyone's pet. The trash was open and the fence was open. The State has a complaint and some fish, but not a hand that put poison out."),
        timeline: [(-30, "{D} complains to {V} about the cats in {D.his} yard."), (0, "Four cats eat fish left near a fence and die within hours."), (2, "A veterinarian confirms antifreeze poisoning and deputies find tainted fish in {D}'s trash.")],
        identified: "Necropsy",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        genders: ["D": .male])

